        application: ['Most of us face Monday as if we were the strongest one in the room. When the news is bad. When the meeting can go either way. When the dark is louder than the promise. Fear grows in an empty room. This verse puts God back in it. Take it deeper: do not leave with the same quiet bargain you walked in with. Let the Word rearrange what you call enough, safe, and later.', 'We treat fear like a fact God can’t touch. The mortgage. The diagnosis. The knock we’re afraid to hear. His help isn’t a mood you work up. It’s his hand, the same hand that keeps his word. Take it deeper: do not leave with the same quiet bargain you walked in with. Let the Word rearrange what you call enough, safe, and later.'],
        invitation: ['Brothers, come. Where are you holding the wall up as if God stepped out? The money. The body. The future of somebody you love. Maybe a fear you smile over. If the Spirit is pressing you, do not wait for a better feeling. Answer him.', 'Brothers, come. What have you been carrying like you’re the only adult in the story? Name it. Then name who is with you. If the Spirit is pressing you, do not wait for a better feeling. Answer him.'],
        closingPrayer: ['Father, thank you for your Word. Plant this truth in us for the week we actually have. Give us courage to obey and mercy when we fail. Through Jesus Christ. Amen.', 'Lord, we have heard you. Now keep us from leaving this room unchanged. Make us doers of the Word. In Jesus’ name. Amen.'],
